{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":49,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 49:1"},"Hear this, all ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["ye"]}," people; give ear, all ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["ye"]}," inhabitants of the world: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 49:2"},"Both low and high, rich and poor, together. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 49:3"},"My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["shall be"]}," of understanding. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 49:4"},"I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 49:5"},"Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["when"]}," the iniquity of my heels shall compass me about? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 49:6"},"They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 49:7"},"None ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of them"]}," can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 49:8"},"(For the redemption of their soul ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," precious, and it ceaseth for ever:) ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 49:9"},"That he should still live for ever, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," not see corruption. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 49:10"},"For he seeth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:10"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PSA 49:11"},"Their inward thought ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is, that"]}," their houses ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["shall continue"]}," for ever, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," their dwelling places to all generations; they call ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["their"]}," lands after their own names. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:11"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PSA 49:12"},"Nevertheless man ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["being"]}," in honour abideth not: he is like the beasts ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," perish. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:12"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PSA 49:13"},"This their way ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:13"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PSA 49:14"},"Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:14"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PSA 49:15"},"But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:15"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PSA 49:16"},"Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:16"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PSA 49:17"},"For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:17"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"PSA 49:18"},"Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["men"]}," will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:18"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"PSA 49:19"},"He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:19"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"PSA 49:20"},"Man ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that is"]}," in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," perish. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 49:20"}]}]}
